## qf-earth | Quick-fire: Earth | earth | 0 | - | ea-earth2
quiz 2 | What's the largest ocean?
* Pacific
o Atlantic
o Indian
o Southern
= It covers about a third of Earth's surface.
> Next

quiz 2 | What's the longest river (by most measurements)?
* The Nile
o The Amazon
o The Yangtze
o The Mississippi
= Some measurements give the Amazon; it depends on where you define the source.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which layer of the Earth is liquid?
* The outer core
o The inner core
o The crust
o The lower mantle
= Convection in the liquid iron outer core generates Earth's magnetic field.
> Next

quiz 3 | What percentage of Earth's water is fresh?
* About 2.5%
o About 25%
o About 50%
o About 0.01%
= Most of that is locked in ice caps and glaciers.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which is the driest non-polar desert?
* The Atacama
o The Sahara
o The Gobi
o The Kalahari
= Some weather stations there have recorded almost no rain for years.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's the deepest point in the ocean?
* The Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench
o The Puerto Rico Trench
o The Java Trench
o The Arctic Basin
= About 10,900 m deep.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which gas makes up most of the greenhouse effect by volume of effect?
* Water vapour
o Carbon dioxide
o Methane
o Ozone
= But water vapour responds to temperature, while CO₂ levels drive the long-term change.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which country has the most active volcanoes?
* Indonesia
o Japan
o Iceland
o Italy
= Around 120 active volcanoes on the Pacific Ring of Fire.
> Next

quiz 4 | Roughly how old is the Earth?
* About 4.5 billion years
o About 13.8 billion years
o About 450 million years
o About 45 billion years
= From radiometric dating of meteorites and the oldest minerals.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which continent has no permanent human population?
* Antarctica
o Australia
o Greenland
o Arctic
= Researchers live there temporarily. Greenland isn't a continent.
> More quick-fire next

## qf-maths2 | Quick-fire: maths 2 | maths | 1 | - | qf-maths
quiz 2 | √144 = ?
* 12
o 14
o 11
o 72
= 12 × 12 = 144.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is 2¹⁰?
* 1,024
o 1,000
o 512
o 2,048
= Why a "kilobyte" was historically 1,024 bytes.
> Next

quiz 3 | Area of a circle with radius 3?
* 9π
o 6π
o 3π
o 12π
= πr².
> Next

quiz 3 | Solve 2x + 6 = 14.
* x = 4
o x = 10
o x = 3
o x = 7
= 2x = 8.
> Next

quiz 3 | Roots of x² − 5x + 6 = 0?
* 2 and 3
o −2 and −3
o 1 and 6
o 5 and 6
= (x − 2)(x − 3).
> Next

quiz 3 | sin(30°) = ?
* 1/2
o √3/2
o 1
o √2/2
= From the 30-60-90 triangle.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is e to 3 decimal places?
* 2.718
o 3.142
o 1.618
o 2.303
= 1.618 is the golden ratio; 2.303 is ln 10.
> Next

quiz 4 | The sum 1 + 2 + … + 100 = ?
* 5,050
o 5,000
o 10,100
o 4,950
= n(n + 1)/2. Gauss is said to have spotted this as a schoolboy.
> Next

quiz 4 | How many diagonals does a hexagon have?
* 9
o 6
o 12
o 15
= n(n − 3)/2.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the determinant of the 2×2 identity matrix?
* 1
o 0
o 2
o 4
= It doesn't change any area.
> Next

quiz 4 | 1/3 + 1/6 = ?
* 1/2
o 2/9
o 1/9
o 2/3
= 2/6 + 1/6 = 3/6.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's 15% of 80?
* 12
o 15
o 8
o 1.2
= 0.15 × 80.
> Quick-fire round four complete
